a good tuesday evening to you thank you  for joining us on 8 news now at 5 i'm  brian loftis  and i'm denise valdez all across the  country millions of americans are  missing appointments for their second  vaccine dose  according to the cdc more than 5 million  skipped their second  pfizer or modernity doses as of early  april a critical component in protecting  people  eight news now reporter victoria saha  joins us now live with why you should  not miss it victoria  the southern nevada health district is  doing everything they can to make it as  easy as possible for you to get  vaccinated  including hosting many pop-up vaccine  clinics like the one here at the  hollywood recreation center on the east  side of the valley  but no matter where you go for your  first dose dose it's  crucial to finish the vaccination  process and get your second dose  the southern nevada health district says  currently 99  000 individuals in clark county are  eligible to get their second dose  but have not gotten it dr mack j khan at  the  current school of medicine says if you  think that you are somewhat protected  with just the first dose you may want to  think again  so the first dose of the vaccine primes  the immune system  or gets it ready for the infection the  second dose or the booster  magnifies that immune response to really  provide  much more protection against a viral  infection  not completing your full vaccination  series also diminishes the state's  efforts to slow the virus  if you are a few weeks behind from your  second dose it's not too late to  schedule your second dose  but you want to do it sooner rather than  later and this location right behind me  at the hollywood recreation center  is taking appointments until 8 pm  tonight and then again tomorrow  4pm until 8 pm reporting live victoria  saha  8 news now
 

